<title>USA: N.J. court workers could face layoffs -- paper.</title>
<headline>N.J. court workers could face layoffs -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>As many as 275 court employees could be laid off if New Jersey does not come up with an additional $9 million in next year's budget, the Star Ledger reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>James Ciancia, administrative director the courts, told the Assembly Appropriations Committee that raising court fees and permit costs could generate about $8.4 million. But lawmakers have been unwilling to introduce that kind of legislation in an election year, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Gov. Christine Whitman has recommended a $346 million budget for the Judiciary for fiscal 1998, which begins July 1. The figure would hold spending at 1997 levels.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
